    "text": "Did you know that if you blend one can of black beans with two eggs, three tablespoons of cocoa powder, a quarter cup of raw honey, and one teaspoon of vanilla, then pour the mixture into a baking pan and bake it for 20 minutes until the top cracks. You end up with rich, fudgy brownies that taste like a bakery made them, but with no flour and no refined sugar. The resistant starch feeds good bacteria in your gut, the fiber slows digestion so your blood sugar stays speedy and you stay full for hours. If you crave something sweet, but you're trying to lose weight, these are genuinely the ones to make. Comment yes if you'd like more recipes like this and follow me so you don't miss the next one."
